  "visualBrief": "Historic Chicago TribuneTower: own native chamfered eight-sided shaft with Indiana limestone raised vertical piers, individually divided recessed glazing/dark horizontal spandrels, elaborate lower Gothic lights/inset bronze doors and pointed west mainportal, original simplified foliate relief/embedded historic fragment patches. Stepped inward central Gothic crown with round-arched glazed lights, eight independent outer buttress piers/actual curved open flying spans/pierced tracery and galleries/clustered ribs/crocketed pinnacles/small abstract gargoyles. Flat upper cap/metal guard/flagpole, no invented spire. Historic tower only; Radio/TV/printingplant/newglasswings/courtyard/newTribuneEast/neighbors/statue/interiors excluded.",
